# ============================================================================
# Phase 7 Scenario 6 — Combination (post-OD linkage + bup expansion + MOUD HIV testing)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Intent: scenarios 2 + 3 + 5 applied together (CALIBRATION_PLAN.md:434), to
# measure interaction effects against the sum of the single arms.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17 — the knob list named `moud.enroll.<window>.prob`, which
# does not exist. Scenario 3's knob is `moud.reinit_prob`. See that template.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DELTAS, all in one file
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   moud.post_overdose_rr                        from scenario 2
#   moud.reinit_prob                             from scenario 3
#   hiv_testing.moud_early_mult / _stable_mult   from scenario 5
#
# Use the SAME values chosen for the individual arms, or the combination is not
# decomposable against them.
#
# SSP (scenario 4) is NOT in this combination per the runbook. Add it only if the
# analysis plan changes, and say so explicitly if you do.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ONE INTERACTION THAT IS NOT OPTIONAL TO THINK ABOUT
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scenarios 2 and 3 both act on the same quantity. moud.py computes
#
#     p_start = moud.reinit_prob x moud.post_overdose_rr   (when recent_overdose)
#
# and then CLAMPS to 1.0. So raising reinit_prob for scenario 3 pushes the
# post-overdose product further into the clamp, and the combination will show
# LESS than the sum of the single arms for a purely mechanical reason — the
# ceiling — rather than because of any epidemiological interaction.
#
# Worked at trial 561, with scenario 2 arm (a) and scenario 3 as recommended:
#
#     scenario 2 alone   0.11833 x 6.59 = 0.780
#     scenario 6         0.24968 x 6.59 = 1.000  (clamped from 1.645)
#
# Report this. Sub-additivity that is really a clamp is the kind of result that
# reads as an epidemiological finding if it is not named as an artefact. If the
# intent is a genuine interaction test, recompute scenario 2's multiplier against
# scenario 3's reinit_prob so the post-overdose linkage PROBABILITY is held at
# 0.78 in both arms:
#
#     post_overdose_rr (combination) = 0.78 / <scenario 3's reinit_prob>
#     worked: 0.78 / 0.24968 = 3.12
#
# Those are two different questions — "both policies at their own settings" vs
# "both policies at a common linkage rate" — and the choice belongs in the paper's
# methods, not in a YAML comment.
#
# ============================================================================
# moud:
#   post_overdose_rr: <FILL IN — from scenario 2, or recomputed; see above>
#   reinit_prob:      <FILL IN — from scenario 3>
# hiv_testing:
#   moud_early_mult:  <FILL IN — from scenario 5>
#   moud_stable_mult: <FILL IN — from scenario 5>
